@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-credit-points-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-s33a-credit-point`
IMPORT `ito-s34-s36-s36a-credits`
IMPORT `ito-credit-points-published-figures`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests for row IL-01. Every expected value below was written from the SOURCE
-- (the sentence of the Ordinance cited beside it, or the Israel Tax
-- Authority's statement cited in ito-credit-points-published-figures.l4) and
-- not read off the code. Where the source leaves a choice, the fork in
-- NOTES.md that settles it is named beside the assertion.
--
-- A failing assertion is a finding: none of these has ever been edited to
-- match what the code computed.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — credit points under ss 33A, 34, 36 and 36A`

§§ `The people in the tests`

-- Four facts per individual, in the order the nouns module declares them.
-- Each case is spelled out in full so the reader can see every fact.

`a resident man` MEANS `an individual` (Individual WITH
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                  IS TRUE
    `a woman`                                              IS FALSE
    `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS FALSE
    `a foreign worker`                                     IS FALSE)

`a resident woman` MEANS `an individual` (Individual WITH
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                  IS TRUE
    `a woman`                                              IS TRUE
    `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS FALSE
    `a foreign worker`                                     IS FALSE)

`a non-resident man` MEANS `an individual` (Individual WITH
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                  IS FALSE
    `a woman`                                              IS FALSE
    `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS FALSE
    `a foreign worker`                                     IS FALSE)

`a non-resident woman` MEANS `an individual` (Individual WITH
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                  IS FALSE
    `a woman`                                              IS TRUE
    `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS FALSE
    `a foreign worker`                                     IS FALSE)

`a resident man who is a foreign worker` MEANS `an individual` (Individual WITH
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                  IS TRUE
    `a woman`                                              IS FALSE
    `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS FALSE
    `a foreign worker`                                     IS TRUE)

`a resident woman who is a foreign worker` MEANS `an individual` (Individual WITH
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                  IS TRUE
    `a woman`                                              IS TRUE
    `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS FALSE
    `a foreign worker`                                     IS TRUE)

`a non-resident man who is a foreign worker` MEANS `an individual` (Individual WITH
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                  IS FALSE
    `a woman`                                              IS FALSE
    `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS FALSE
    `a foreign worker`                                     IS TRUE)

`a non-resident woman who is a foreign worker` MEANS `an individual` (Individual WITH
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                  IS FALSE
    `a woman`                                              IS TRUE
    `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS FALSE
    `a foreign worker`                                     IS TRUE)

`a man resident in the Area, not an Israeli citizen and not an Israeli resident` MEANS `an individual` (Individual WITH
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                  IS FALSE
    `a woman`                                              IS FALSE
    `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS TRUE
    `a foreign worker`                                     IS FALSE)

`a woman resident in the Area, not an Israeli citizen and not an Israeli resident` MEANS `an individual` (Individual WITH
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                  IS FALSE
    `a woman`                                              IS TRUE
    `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS TRUE
    `a foreign worker`                                     IS FALSE)

-- Resident in Israel for the tax year AND recorded as an Area resident who is
-- not a citizen: s 34 reaches such a person directly, so s 48 is not needed.
-- (0.2.0) The facts contradict each other: s 48 takes "אזרח ישראלי" from
-- s 3A(a), whose para (2) makes every Israeli resident an "Israeli citizen"
-- (line 457), so no Israeli resident is an Area resident who is not one. The
-- fixture is kept to show that a resident's points do not turn on the Area
-- fact, whatever it says.
`a man resident in Israel who is also recorded as an Area resident and not a citizen` MEANS `an individual` (Individual WITH
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                  IS TRUE
    `a woman`                                              IS FALSE
    `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS TRUE
    `a foreign worker`                                     IS FALSE)

`a company` MEANS `a body of persons`

§§ `Section 34 — illustrations`
-- line 1570: בחישוב המס של יחיד שהיה תושב ישראל בשנת המס יובאו בחשבון שתי נקודות זיכוי.

-- Both limbs met: an individual, resident in the tax year. Two points.
#ASSERT `section 34 applies to` `a resident man`
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 34 for` `a resident man` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 34 for` `a resident woman` EQUALS 2

-- The residence limb fails. The section gives nothing.
#ASSERT NOT `section 34 applies to` `a non-resident man`
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 34 for` `a non-resident man` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 34 for` `a non-resident woman` EQUALS 0

-- The individual limb fails: a company is not a "יחיד".
#ASSERT NOT `section 34, as written, applies to` `a company`
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 34 for` `a company` EQUALS 0

-- s 48A: regulations may take the credit away from a foreign worker "even if
-- treated as a resident". The sentence of s 34 is met, the answer is not known.
#ASSERT `section 34, as written, applies to` `a resident man who is a foreign worker`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 34 for` `a resident man who is a foreign worker` BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"

-- s 48A can only take away. Where s 34 gives nothing, the answer stands.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 34 for` `a non-resident man who is a foreign worker` EQUALS 0

-- s 48: an order may apply s 34 to an Area resident who is not an Israeli
-- citizen "as if" an Israeli resident. Not encoded, so the model declines.
#ASSERT NOT `section 34, as written, applies to` `a man resident in the Area, not an Israeli citizen and not an Israeli resident`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 34 for` `a man resident in the Area, not an Israeli citizen and not an Israeli resident` BECAUSE "section 48 and the order made under it are not encoded in this model"

-- An Israeli resident needs no s 48 order: s 34 reaches him directly. (0.2.0)
-- The Area fact here cannot be true of a resident (s 3A(a)(2), line 457).
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 34 for` `a man resident in Israel who is also recorded as an Area resident and not a citizen` EQUALS 2

§§ `Section 36 — illustrations`
-- line 1594: בחישוב המס של יחיד תושב ישראל תובא בחשבון 1⁄4 נקודת זיכוי כזיכוי נסיעה.

-- A resident individual: a quarter point, with no condition of earning or
-- travel (fork F2).
#ASSERT `section 36 applies to` `a resident man`
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36 for` `a resident man` EQUALS 0.25
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36 for` `a resident woman` EQUALS 1/4

-- Not resident; not an individual.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36 for` `a non-resident man` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36 for` `a company` EQUALS 0

-- s 48A and s 48, as for s 34.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 36 for` `a resident man who is a foreign worker` BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36 for` `a non-resident man who is a foreign worker` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 36 for` `a man resident in the Area, not an Israeli citizen and not an Israeli resident` BECAUSE "section 48 and the order made under it are not encoded in this model"

§§ `Section 36A — illustrations`
-- line 1597: בחישוב המס של אשה תובא בחשבון 1⁄2 נקודת זיכוי.

-- A woman: half a point.
#ASSERT `section 36A applies to` `a resident woman`
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36A for` `a resident woman` EQUALS 0.5

-- The sentence carries no residence limb (fork F1).
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36A for` `a non-resident woman` EQUALS 1/2

-- Not a woman; not an individual.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36A for` `a resident man` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36A for` `a company` EQUALS 0

-- s 48A reaches s 36A ("הוראות פרק זה לענין זיכויים"); s 48 does not name it.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 36A for` `a resident woman who is a foreign worker` BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 36A for` `a non-resident woman who is a foreign worker` BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36A for` `a non-resident man who is a foreign worker` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36A for` `a woman resident in the Area, not an Israeli citizen and not an Israeli resident` EQUALS 1/2

§§ `Aggregates — illustrations`
-- line 4864: מסכום נקודות הזיכוי שעל פי סעיפים 34 ו־36

-- Two points and a quarter, for any resident individual.
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34 and 36 for` `a resident man` EQUALS 2.25
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34 and 36 for` `a resident woman` EQUALS 2.25
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34 and 36 for` `a non-resident woman` EQUALS 0

-- Adding s 36A's half point for a woman.
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `a resident man` EQUALS 2.25
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `a resident woman` EQUALS 2.75
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `a non-resident woman` EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `a company` EQUALS 0

-- A total that needs a refused part is itself refused, never a partial sum.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `a woman resident in the Area, not an Israeli citizen and not an Israeli resident` BECAUSE "section 48 and the order made under it are not encoded in this model"

§§ `Section 33A — illustrations`
-- line 1563: ”נקודת זיכוי“ – סכום של 504 שקלים חדשים ... לשנת מס, צמוד למדד כאמור בסעיף 120א, המקוזז כנגד המס לאותה שנה;

#ASSERT `the amount of a credit point as written in section 33A, before indexation` EQUALS 504

-- The Israel Tax Authority, tax year 2025: one point is worth NIS 2,904, and
-- "the credit given is the product of the number of credit points and the
-- value of one credit point" ([itc135-2025] p. 4).
#ASSERT `the amount of` 1 `credit points at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 2904
#ASSERT `the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `a resident man` `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 6534
#ASSERT `the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `a resident woman` `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 7986
#ASSERT `the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `a non-resident woman` `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 1452
#ASSERT `the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `a company` `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 0

-- Using the published figure rather than typing it.
#ASSERT `the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `a resident woman` `at a credit-point value of` (`the value of one credit point published by the Israel Tax Authority for tax year` 2025) EQUALS 7986

-- "המקוזז כנגד המס לאותה שנה": the amount comes off that year's tax, and a
-- set-off takes the tax to nothing at most (fork F5).
#ASSERT `the tax for the year after setting off` 6534 `against` 10000 EQUALS 3466
#ASSERT `the tax for the year after setting off` 7986 `against` 7986 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the tax for the year after setting off` 7986 `against` 5000 EQUALS 0

-- line 1564: ומחולק בשנים עשר
-- An allowance point is the adjusted 1996 figure divided by twelve. The two
-- inputs below are HYPOTHETICAL: they are the figures in the Wikisource
-- editorial notes at lines 1563-1564 (an aid, not law), chosen because the
-- same notes give the allowance points they should produce (235; 242).
#ASSERT `the amount of an allowance point, given` 2820 EQUALS 235
#ASSERT `the amount of an allowance point, given` 2904 EQUALS 242

§§ `Published figures — illustrations`

#ASSERT `the value of one credit point published by the Israel Tax Authority for tax year` 2025 EQUALS 2904
#ASSERT REFUSED `the value of one credit point published by the Israel Tax Authority for tax year` 2024 BECAUSE "no annual credit-point value published by the Israel Tax Authority for this tax year has been sourced in this encoding"
#ASSERT `the monthly credit-point figure in the Israel Tax Authority's withholding booklet for tax year` 2024 EQUALS 242
#ASSERT `the monthly credit-point figure in the Israel Tax Authority's withholding booklet for tax year` 2025 EQUALS 242
#ASSERT `the monthly credit-point figure in the Israel Tax Authority's withholding booklet for tax year` 2026 EQUALS 242
#ASSERT REFUSED `the monthly credit-point figure in the Israel Tax Authority's withholding booklet for tax year` 2023 BECAUSE "no monthly credit-point figure published by the Israel Tax Authority for this tax year has been sourced in this encoding"

-- Two Authority publications for 2025 agree: twelve monthly figures make the
-- annual one. A check on the sources, not a rule of the Ordinance.
#ASSERT 12 TIMES (`the monthly credit-point figure in the Israel Tax Authority's withholding booklet for tax year` 2025) EQUALS `the value of one credit point published by the Israel Tax Authority for tax year` 2025

-- ===========================================================================
-- 0.2.0 (2026-10-08, BACKLOG IL-14): the year-aware rules over a
-- `Taxpayer in a tax year`. Every expected value below was worked out from
-- the source before the rules were run; the working is in the comment beside
-- each group and in NOTES.md, version 0.2.0.
--
-- The year limits, from each section's amendment list (assumed, not ruled):
-- the deposited text governs a tax year beginning after the Hebrew year of
-- the last listed amendment has ended.
--   s 34   last תשל״ה־2  (5735 ended September 1975)  first year 1976
--   s 36   last תשל״ז־4  (5737 ended September 1977)  first year 1978
--   s 36A  last תשנ״ו    (5756 ended September 1996)  first year 1997
--   s 33A  last תשס״ד־2  (5764 ended September 2004)  first year 2005
--   s 3A   last תשע״ו־22 (5776 ended October 2016)    first year 2017
--   s 48A  enacted תשס״ג־3 (5763 began 7 September 2002): refused from 2002
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Tax years and section 3A(f) — the cases (0.2.0)`

-- A person in a tax year with neither s 3A(f) fact: the two facts are FALSE.
GIVEN p IS A Person
      y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
`the case of` p `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` y MEANS `Taxpayer in a tax year` WITH
    `the taxpayer`                                     IS p
    `the tax year`                                     IS y
    `an Israeli citizen who is a resident of the Area` IS FALSE
    `an Israeli citizen who operates in the Area`      IS FALSE

-- s 3A(f), limb (i): an Israeli citizen who is a resident of the Area, and
-- not an Israeli resident under s 1. The individual's own four facts are a
-- non-resident's; the limb is carried by the case.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
`an Israeli citizen resident in the Area, a man, in tax year` y MEANS `Taxpayer in a tax year` WITH
    `the taxpayer`                                     IS `a non-resident man`
    `the tax year`                                     IS y
    `an Israeli citizen who is a resident of the Area` IS TRUE
    `an Israeli citizen who operates in the Area`      IS FALSE

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
`an Israeli citizen resident in the Area, a woman, in tax year` y MEANS `Taxpayer in a tax year` WITH
    `the taxpayer`                                     IS `a non-resident woman`
    `the tax year`                                     IS y
    `an Israeli citizen who is a resident of the Area` IS TRUE
    `an Israeli citizen who operates in the Area`      IS FALSE

-- s 3A(f), limb (ii): an Israeli citizen who operates in the Area, resident
-- neither in Israel under s 1 nor in the Area.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
`an Israeli citizen operating in the Area, a man, in tax year` y MEANS `Taxpayer in a tax year` WITH
    `the taxpayer`                                     IS `a non-resident man`
    `the tax year`                                     IS y
    `an Israeli citizen who is a resident of the Area` IS FALSE
    `an Israeli citizen who operates in the Area`      IS TRUE

-- Contradictory facts: an Israeli citizen resident in the Area (limb (i))
-- who is also recorded as a resident of the Area who is NOT an Israeli
-- citizen (the s 48 fact).
`a man entered as both an Israeli citizen and not one, resident in the Area, in 2026` MEANS `Taxpayer in a tax year` WITH
    `the taxpayer`                                     IS `a man resident in the Area, not an Israeli citizen and not an Israeli resident`
    `the tax year`                                     IS 2026
    `an Israeli citizen who is a resident of the Area` IS TRUE
    `an Israeli citizen who operates in the Area`      IS FALSE

-- An Israeli resident under s 1 who is ALSO an Israeli citizen operating in
-- the Area: s 34 reaches such a person directly, so s 3A is not consulted.
`a resident man who also operates in the Area, in 2010` MEANS `Taxpayer in a tax year` WITH
    `the taxpayer`                                     IS `a resident man`
    `the tax year`                                     IS 2010
    `an Israeli citizen who is a resident of the Area` IS FALSE
    `an Israeli citizen who operates in the Area`      IS TRUE

-- A body of persons controlled by an Israeli citizen is itself an "Israeli
-- citizen" (s 3A(a)(4), line 459); s 3A(f) may treat it as resident, but
-- ss 34 and 36 speak only of a "יחיד".
`a company controlled by an Israeli citizen, operating in the Area, in 2010` MEANS `Taxpayer in a tax year` WITH
    `the taxpayer`                                     IS `a company`
    `the tax year`                                     IS 2010
    `an Israeli citizen who is a resident of the Area` IS FALSE
    `an Israeli citizen who operates in the Area`      IS TRUE

§§ `Section 3A(f) — illustrations (0.2.0)`
-- line 471: (ו) בכפוף להוראות סעיף זה, יחולו על אזרח ישראלי שהוא תושב אזור או פועל באזור, הוראות פקודה זו כאילו היה תושב ישראל
-- Treated "as if" an Israeli resident, the individual meets the residence
-- limb of s 34 (line 1570) and of s 36 (line 1594): 2 points and 1/4.
-- s 36A has no residence limb, so it gives what it gives anyone: 1/2 to a
-- woman, 0 to a man. Totals: a man 2 + 1/4 + 0 = 9/4; a woman 2 + 1/4 + 1/2 = 11/4.
-- These are the independent tester's S09a and S09b (DECIDED-ANSWERS.md).

-- Limb (i), "אזרח ישראלי שהוא תושב אזור", tax year 2026.
#ASSERT `section 34 applies in the tax year of` (`an Israeli citizen resident in the Area, a man, in tax year` 2026)
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of` (`an Israeli citizen resident in the Area, a man, in tax year` 2026) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36 in the tax year of` (`an Israeli citizen resident in the Area, a man, in tax year` 2026) EQUALS 1/4
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36A in the tax year of` (`an Israeli citizen resident in the Area, a man, in tax year` 2026) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` (`an Israeli citizen resident in the Area, a man, in tax year` 2026) EQUALS 9/4
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` (`an Israeli citizen resident in the Area, a woman, in tax year` 2026) EQUALS 11/4

-- Limb (ii), "או פועל באזור", tax year 2026.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of` (`an Israeli citizen operating in the Area, a man, in tax year` 2026) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36 in the tax year of` (`an Israeli citizen operating in the Area, a man, in tax year` 2026) EQUALS 1/4
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34 and 36 in the tax year of` (`an Israeli citizen operating in the Area, a man, in tax year` 2026) EQUALS 9/4

-- The same individual without the s 3A(f) fact is a plain non-resident: 0.
-- This is what 0.1.0 answered for both limbs, with no diagnostic.
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a non-resident man` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 2026) EQUALS 0

-- The text of s 3A is held for tax years from 2017 only. For 2016 the
-- s 3A(f) route refuses; s 36A, which does not need it, still answers.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of` (`an Israeli citizen resident in the Area, a man, in tax year` 2016) BECAUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 3A for a tax year before 2017"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 36 in the tax year of` (`an Israeli citizen operating in the Area, a man, in tax year` 2016) BECAUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 3A for a tax year before 2017"
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36A in the tax year of` (`an Israeli citizen resident in the Area, a woman, in tax year` 2016) EQUALS 1/2
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of` (`an Israeli citizen resident in the Area, a man, in tax year` 2017) EQUALS 2

-- A resident under s 1 needs no s 3A(f): 2 points even in 2010.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of` `a resident man who also operates in the Area, in 2010` EQUALS 2

-- Contradictory facts about citizenship: s 3A(f) would give 2, s 48 would
-- refuse; the rule declines and says why.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of` `a man entered as both an Israeli citizen and not one, resident in the Area, in 2026` BECAUSE "the facts say the taxpayer both is and is not an Israeli citizen within section 3A(a)"

-- A body of persons is not a "יחיד", whatever s 3A(f) says of it, so s 3A's
-- year limit (2017) is never reached: 0 in 2010 as in any year.
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` `a company controlled by an Israeli citizen, operating in the Area, in 2010` EQUALS 0

§§ `Tax years — illustrations (0.2.0)`

-- The years the deposited text governs give the year-free answers: 2026 and
-- 2024 (the tester's S38 and S39), 9/4 for a resident man, 11/4 for a woman.
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident man` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 2026) EQUALS 9/4
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident man` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 2024) EQUALS 9/4
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident woman` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 2026) EQUALS 11/4
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a non-resident woman` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 2026) EQUALS 1/2
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a company` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 2026) EQUALS 0

-- Tax year 1990 (the tester's S41): ss 34 and 36 were last amended in 5735
-- and 5737, so their text governs 1990: 2 and 1/4. s 36A was last amended
-- in 5756, after 1990, so its 1990 text is not held: refused, and so is any
-- total that includes it.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident woman` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 1990) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36 in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident woman` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 1990) EQUALS 1/4
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34 and 36 in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident woman` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 1990) EQUALS 9/4
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 36A in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident woman` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 1990) BECAUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 36A for a tax year before 1997"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident woman` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 1990) BECAUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 36A for a tax year before 1997"

-- The s 36A boundary: 5756 ended in September 1996, so 1996 is refused and
-- 1997 answered.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 36A in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident woman` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 1996) BECAUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 36A for a tax year before 1997"
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36A in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident woman` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 1997) EQUALS 1/2

-- Tax year 1970 (the tester's S40): before both ss 34 and 36 took their
-- present text. Refused, whatever the person.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident man` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 1970) BECAUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 34 for a tax year before 1976"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 36 in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident man` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 1970) BECAUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 36 for a tax year before 1978"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a non-resident man` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 1970) BECAUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 34 for a tax year before 1976"

-- The s 34 and s 36 boundaries: 5735 ended in September 1975 (s 34 from
-- 1976), 5737 in September 1977 (s 36 from 1978).
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident man` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 1975) BECAUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 34 for a tax year before 1976"
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident man` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 1976) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 36 in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident man` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 1977) BECAUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 36 for a tax year before 1978"
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36 in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident man` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 1978) EQUALS 1/4

-- Tax year 1960 (the tester's S42): every section refuses.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident woman` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 1960) BECAUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 34 for a tax year before 1976"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 36 in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident woman` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 1960) BECAUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 36 for a tax year before 1978"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 36A in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident woman` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 1960) BECAUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 36A for a tax year before 1997"

§§ `Sections 48A and 48, for a tax year — illustrations (0.2.0)`

-- s 48A was enacted in 5763 (the amendment list at line 1810 is תשס״ג־3), a
-- Hebrew year that began on 7 September 2002, so tax year 2002 is the first
-- it could reach. From 2002 a foreign worker whom a section would credit is
-- refused: s 48A and whatever regulations stood under it that year are not
-- encoded (the lead's choice, 2026-10-08, assumed, not ruled). Before 2002
-- s 48A did not exist, so the section's own answer stands.
-- (These assertions were first written, and run, for the lead's earlier date
-- of 2014; they were rewritten from the revised choice before being run again.)

-- Tax year 2001: a resident foreign worker gets what ss 34 and 36 give, 2 and
-- 1/4; a woman also s 36A's 1/2 (its text governs from 1997), so
-- 2 + 1/4 + 1/2 = 11/4; a non-resident foreign-worker woman, s 36A's 1/2.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident man who is a foreign worker` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 2001) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36 in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident man who is a foreign worker` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 2001) EQUALS 1/4
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident woman who is a foreign worker` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 2001) EQUALS 11/4
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36A in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a non-resident woman who is a foreign worker` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 2001) EQUALS 1/2
-- Tax year 1990: the same, for s 34.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident man who is a foreign worker` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 1990) EQUALS 2

-- Tax year 2002 on: refused, as the year-free rules refuse in every year.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident man who is a foreign worker` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 2002) BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 36 in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident man who is a foreign worker` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 2002) BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 36A in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident woman who is a foreign worker` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 2002) BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
-- 2013 lies in the window the earlier choice (2014) would have answered.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident man who is a foreign worker` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 2013) BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 36A in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a non-resident woman who is a foreign worker` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 2013) BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 36A in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a non-resident woman who is a foreign worker` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 2026) BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
-- s 48A can only take away: where the section gives nothing, 0 in any year.
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a non-resident man who is a foreign worker` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 2026) EQUALS 0

-- s 48 is not dated: an Area resident who is not an Israeli citizen and not
-- an Israeli resident is refused in every year the section's text governs.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a man resident in the Area, not an Israeli citizen and not an Israeli resident` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 1990) BECAUSE "section 48 and the order made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 36 in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a man resident in the Area, not an Israeli citizen and not an Israeli resident` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 2026) BECAUSE "section 48 and the order made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36A in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a woman resident in the Area, not an Israeli citizen and not an Israeli resident` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 2026) EQUALS 1/2

§§ `Section 33A, for a tax year — illustrations (0.2.0)`
-- s 33A's text is held for tax years from 2005 (5764 ended September 2004).

-- One point at the 2025 value is the 2025 value: 1 x 2,904 = 2,904.
#ASSERT `the amount of` 1 `credit points at a credit-point value of` 2904 `in tax year` 2025 EQUALS 2904
#ASSERT REFUSED `the amount of` 1 `credit points at a credit-point value of` 2904 `in tax year` 2004 BECAUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 33A for a tax year before 2005"
-- A HYPOTHETICAL value of 2,000 for 2005, to show the boundary answers:
-- 9/4 x 2,000 = 4,500.
#ASSERT `the amount of` (9/4) `credit points at a credit-point value of` 2000 `in tax year` 2005 EQUALS 4500

-- The set-off: 10,000 - 6,534 = 3,466 (fork F5), for 2025; refused for 2004.
#ASSERT `the tax for the year after setting off` 6534 `against` 10000 `in tax year` 2025 EQUALS 3466
#ASSERT REFUSED `the tax for the year after setting off` 6534 `against` 10000 `in tax year` 2004 BECAUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 33A for a tax year before 2005"

-- The allowance point, from the HYPOTHETICAL input of the 0.1.0 tests:
-- 2,904 / 12 = 242.
#ASSERT `the amount of an allowance point, given` 2904 `in tax year` 2025 EQUALS 242
#ASSERT REFUSED `the amount of an allowance point, given` 2904 `in tax year` 2004 BECAUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 33A for a tax year before 2005"

§§ `The @export, for a tax year — illustrations (0.2.0)`

-- [itc135-2025] p. 4: one point is NIS 2,904 in 2025.
-- A resident woman: 11/4 x 2,904 = 7,986. A resident man: 9/4 x 2,904 = 6,534.
#ASSERT `the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident woman` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 2025) `at a credit-point value of` (`the value of one credit point published by the Israel Tax Authority for tax year` 2025) EQUALS 7986
#ASSERT `the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident man` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 2025) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 6534

-- s 3A(f) through the @export: limb (i) a man 6,534, a woman 7,986;
-- limb (ii) a man 6,534. (0.1.0's @export answered 0, 1,452 and 0.)
#ASSERT `the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` (`an Israeli citizen resident in the Area, a man, in tax year` 2025) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 6534
#ASSERT `the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` (`an Israeli citizen resident in the Area, a woman, in tax year` 2025) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 7986
#ASSERT `the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` (`an Israeli citizen operating in the Area, a man, in tax year` 2025) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 6534

-- 2004: ss 34, 36 and 36A all govern it, but s 33A's text is held only from
-- 2005, and the amount is s 33A's: refused.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` (`the case of` `a resident man` `, with no section 3A(f) fact, in tax year` 2004) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 BECAUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 33A for a tax year before 2005"
